+## Independent evidence (own computation, no project code reused)
+
+From-scratch exact adaptive transitive-closure minimax plus subset-DP linear-extension
+count, written this pass at `/tmp/opencode/ref_two_fronts_20261121.py`. I found and
+fixed TWO bugs in my own evaluator before trusting any number: (1) incomplete
+incremental transitive-closure propagation after adding an order edge — replaced by
+full closure recomputation; (2) a disjoint-union index shift: for `A_m ⊔ B` with B on
+b nodes, B node i must map to combined index m+i, not i. Post-fix sanity checks:
+`S(n)=0,0,1,3,5,7,10` for n=0..6 and `F(C_b)=0`.
+
+- Insertion front: `I(a,1)=F(A_a ⊔ C_1)=1,3,5,7,10` for a=1..5, equal to `S(a+1)`.
+  Collapse at b=1 confirmed: a uniform poly(a+b) evaluator for I puts `S_unary` in
+  FP, i.e. SORT-BOUND-U in P — the flagship open problem, not a new independent
+  frontier. My own count gives O(N^2) distinct length-N strings in `L_I` (sparser
+  than the front's O(N^3)), so many-one counting-class hardness does not transfer
+  without an encoding-preserving reduction.
+- Chain-uniqueness front: T0 re-derived by hand and sound — an information-tight
+  host with `e(B)=2^k` has `F(B)=k`; T1 (chain extremality) gives
+  `F(B ⊔ A_1) <= k+ceil(log2(b+1))`; the information lower bound gives
+  `ceil(log2(e(B)(b+1)))=k+ceil(log2(b+1))`; hence equality and
+  `delta(A_1,B)=ceil(log2(b+1))=delta(A_1,C_b)`. Exact minimax confirms the
+  `Vcap_b` family (e=2, F=1, non-chain): `delta(A_1,Vcap_b)=2,3,3,3,3,4` for
+  b=3..8, matching `ceil(log2(b+1))`. Uniqueness refuted by an infinite family;
+  T1 extremality intact. No complexity-class consequence.
+
+Both fronts honestly report NO theorem completion; S(n) and SORT-BOUND-U remain OPEN.
